    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d993">

                <pb facs="1340" n="1330" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.4061 Motion Pictures/7–3145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-31T08:00:00+07:00">July 31, 1945—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1256. Your No. 1111, July 17, 7 p.m. not received by the Embassy until July 28, 4
                    p.m. We have advised the Ministry of Finance of the acceptance by the Hays
                    Organization of the proposal outlined to you [in] Embassy’s telegram 1161, July
                    13. We have not notified local representatives either of negotiations or results
                    thereof. We assume <pb facs="1341" n="1331" xml:id="pg1331"/> they will be
                    instructed by their principals in U. S. If we are to take further action, please
                    advise by cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
